  "Number": 7,
  "Question": "The sum of all the integers between \\(50\\) and \\(350\\) which end in \\(1\\) is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(5880\\)",
    "B": "\\(5539\\)",
    "C": "\\(5208\\)",
    "D": "\\(4877\\)",
    "E": "\\(4566\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Consecutive integers ending in \\(1\\) are \\(10\\) apart. Thus all the required integers, in increasing order, are\n\\[\n51,61,71,\\ldots,341.\n\\]\nThere are\n\\[\n\\frac{341-51}{10}=29\n\\]\ngaps, so there are \\(30\\) numbers.\n\nPair the smallest with the largest, the next smallest with the next largest, and continue. Each pair sums to \\(51+341=392\\): increasing the smaller term by \\(10\\) decreases its partner by \\(10\\). The \\(30\\) numbers form \\(15\\) disjoint pairs, using every number exactly once. Their sum is therefore\n\\[\n15\\cdot392=\\boxed{5880},\n\\]\nchoice A.",
